text:
How to use the tokens
Copy two things into your project — no npm, no build step:

theme/tokens.css — every token as a CSS custom property (--ncdpi-*), plus the @font-face for Source Sans Pro.
theme/fonts/ — the two self-hosted Source Sans variable-font files (SIL Open Font License; no third-party requests, works on intranet).

Then reference semantic tokens in your styles:
.my-panel {
  background: var(--ncdpi-surface-raised);
  color: var(--ncdpi-on-surface-raised);
  border-radius: var(--ncdpi-radius-lg);
  box-shadow: var(--ncdpi-shadow-raised);
  padding: var(--ncdpi-space-md);
}
Use the semantic tier, not the primitives. Semantic names are mode-neutral (surface, not white) so a future dark mode is a value map, not a rebuild — and every semantic pairing below is contrast-validated on every build (see the contrast grid).

Header & footer — .ncdpi-header / .ncdpi-footer
The brand band. The logo drops into the brand slot as an &lt;img&gt; — use a white/reversed mark on the navy; the logo page covers which file, sizing, and alt text. The component only reserves the slot.



      NC Department of Public Instruction
      Educator Preparation Data



      Questions? Contact the data team ·
      Data current as of August 2026



&lt;header class="ncdpi-header"&gt;
  &lt;span class="ncdpi-header__brand"&gt;&lt;img src="…white logo…" alt="NC DPI"&gt;
    NC Department of Public Instruction&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="ncdpi-header__tagline"&gt;Educator Preparation Data&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;
When to use. Standalone HTML pages, dashboards, and apps that need to say whose they are — the style-guide site itself keeps Quarto’s navbar. Links inside the bands are white and underlined: the navy band is the one place link blue can’t go.
Definition of done. &lt;header&gt;/&lt;footer&gt; landmarks, not divs · white on navy validated (on-surface-brand) · logo &lt;img&gt; carries alt text · tagline dim measured 11.1:1 (AAA headroom).

Tabs — .ncdpi-tabs
The one component that ships behavior: theme/ncdpi-ds.js (optional third file, vanilla, ~100 lines) wires the WAI-ARIA tabs pattern. Without JS the panels simply stack — degraded, never broken.



      Districts
      Counties
      SBE regions

    115 local education agencies, matched by name, code, or official name.
    100 counties, matched by name, DPI code (1–100), or FIPS.
    8 State Board of Education regions, matched by name or number.


&lt;div class="ncdpi-tabs" data-ncdpi-tabs&gt;
  &lt;div class="ncdpi-tabs__list" aria-label="Geography"&gt;
    &lt;button class="ncdpi-tabs__tab" data-panel="tab-districts"&gt;Districts&lt;/button&gt;
    …
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="ncdpi-tabs__panel" id="tab-districts"&gt;…&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;script src="theme/ncdpi-ds.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
When to use. Alternate views of the same thing (geographies of one dataset, code/preview of one example). Not for sequential steps (that’s a wizard) and not for unrelated content (those are pages). If users need to compare two panels side by side, tabs are the wrong pattern.
Definition of done. Arrow/Home/End keys move selection (roving tabindex) · roles and aria-selected set by the JS, never claimed in static markup · panel focusable · selected state marked by more than color (the 3px underline + text-color shift).

Breadcrumb — .ncdpi-breadcrumb



      Home
      Design system
      Components



&lt;nav class="ncdpi-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"&gt;
  &lt;ol&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="/"&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="/data/"&gt;Data & Reports&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li aria-current="page"&gt;Graduation rates&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/nav&gt;
When to use. Three or more levels of real hierarchy. The current page is plain text with aria-current="page", never a link; the › separator is CSS-generated so screen readers don’t read it as content.
Definition of done. &lt;nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"&gt; + &lt;ol&gt; · separator out of the accessibility tree · current page not focusable.

Skip link — .ncdpi-skip-link
Promoted from the style-guide site (it’s been live since session 20 — WCAG 2.4.1). First focusable element on the page, hidden until focused.


    Skip to main content
    Click into this frame and press Tab — the link drops in from the top edge.



&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;a href="#main" class="ncdpi-skip-link"&gt;Skip to main content&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;header class="ncdpi-header"&gt;…&lt;/header&gt;
  &lt;main id="main"&gt;…&lt;/main&gt;
When to use. Every page with repeated navigation before the content — which is every page. Point it at the &lt;main&gt; element’s id.
Definition of done. First element in the DOM · visible on focus with the ring · target id exists (a dead skip link is worse than none).

Chart frame — .ncdpi-chartframe
The C2/C7 wrapper for charts embedded in pages and apps — and the D2 boundary’s other worked example: everything in this frame is chart-world text (Arial, chart-text colors, the dataviz guide’s pt sizes), because the frame belongs to the chart, not the page.


    Sandhills trails the state in grad rate
    4-year cohort graduation rate by SBE region, 2025









    Source: NC School Report Cards, 2025. Demonstration data.


&lt;figure class="ncdpi-chartframe"&gt;
  &lt;div class="ncdpi-chartframe__title"&gt;Message title, not a topic label&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="ncdpi-chartframe__subtitle"&gt;Measure, population, year — the contract&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="ncdpi-chartframe__body"&gt;&lt;!-- the chart --&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="ncdpi-chartframe__source"&gt;Source: …&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
When to use. Any chart dropped into an app or HTML page (the map-maker retrofit is the intended first consumer). Title states the message; subtitle is the contract (measure, population, year); source line always (C7); all four share the left edge (C2). On the style-guide site itself, chart-loader.js already renders this structure for Vega specs — this class packages the same anatomy for everything else.
Definition of done. All text Arial at the chart sizes (14pt title, 11pt subtitle/source as px) · shared left edge, no centered titles · source line present · the chart body carries its own alt text (role="img" + label, or a companion table).

Form basics — .ncdpi-field
Deliberately minimal (label + control + help + error). Form-heavy coverage is out of scope until adoption demands it.



      Goal value
      The value the darkest map color should represent — often 100.



      Reporting year

      Error: enter a year between 2015 and 2026.



&lt;div class="ncdpi-field ncdpi-field--error"&gt;
  &lt;label class="ncdpi-field__label" for="year"&gt;Reporting year&lt;/label&gt;
  &lt;input class="ncdpi-input" id="year" aria-describedby="year-error" aria-invalid="true"&gt;
  &lt;p class="ncdpi-field__error" id="year-error"&gt;Error: enter a year between 2015 and 2026.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
When to use. The occasional input a data product needs (a goal value, a filter, an email field) — not full multi-step forms. Error messages name the problem and the fix, in words (“Error: enter a year between 2015 and 2026”), never just a red border.
Definition of done. Real &lt;label for&gt; on every control · help and error text wired via aria-describedby · aria-invalid on the failed control · error color never the only signal (the message text is) · border ≥3:1 in both states.

On our surfaces






The two SVGs above ship with this site (assets/ncdpi-logo-blue.svg, assets/ncdpi-logo-white.svg) and are byte-identical to the kit’s svgs/ folder — copy them into a consuming project as they are. On the navy header band, the white version is the only correct pick: the blue logo disappears against surface-brand, and no token pairing will rescue it.
In the header component, the logo drops into the brand slot:
&lt;header class="ncdpi-header"&gt;
  &lt;span class="ncdpi-header__brand"&gt;
    &lt;img src="assets/ncdpi-logo-white.svg" alt="NC Department of Public Instruction"
         style="height:32px; width:auto;"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="ncdpi-header__tagline"&gt;Educator Preparation Data&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;
